---
/**
 * A short list of published work cited inside a talk write-up.
 *
 * It exists because a run of six papers set as ordinary prose paragraphs turns
 * into a wall: the same four facts repeat in a different order each time and
 * nothing lines up, so a reader scanning for the one in their own field has to
 * read all of them. As rows, the four facts sit in the same place every time.
 *
 * It wraps `Paper` entries as children rather than taking a list of objects,
 * because that keeps the entries readable in the write-up itself, where they
 * are read far more often than they are edited.
 *
 * @example
 * ```mdx
 * <Papers>
 *   <Paper name="MicroCycle" org="Novartis, Basel" venue="J. Med. Chem." year="2024" doi="10.1021/acs.jmedchem.3c02029">
 *     Plate-based micro-scale chemistry, automated purification.
 *   </Paper>
 * </Papers>
 * ```
 */
---

{/* A plain list, because these are six items of one kind rather than six cards. */}
<ul class="talk-papers">
  <slot />
</ul>

<style>
  .talk-papers {
    margin-block: 1.75rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--color-primary);
  }
</style>
